{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceASpechtCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceASpechtCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtFinrankWired","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyOV","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OVTopAssembly"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.pieceA_hook_sq_eq_content_sq_add_n_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.pieceA_hook_sq_eq_content_sq_add_n_sq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceASpechtCharacter.lean#L91-L100","doc":"Piece A fundamental identity (representation-theoretic route):\n`Σ_c h_c² = Σ_c c(c)² + n²`.\nHere we state the equivalence between the representation-theoretic evaluation\nand the combinatorial formula `sumSqHooks_eq_sumSqContents_add_sq`. \nThe list `l` corresponds to the row lengths of the partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.trace_centralC2_regular_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.trace_centralC2_regular_rep","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceASpechtCharacter.lean#L70-L89","doc":"The central element `C_2` evaluated on the full group algebra is given by \na sum of dimensions and squared contents, bridging representation theory to hooks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.trace_centralC2_specht_module","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.trace_centralC2_specht_module","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceASpechtCharacter.lean#L44-L68","doc":"The trace of `centralC2` on the Specht module `S^μ`.\nSince `centralC2` acts by the scalar `contentSqSum μ` on the Specht module,\nthe restricted operator is `(contentSqSum μ) • id`, so its trace evaluates to\n`contentSqSum μ * dim(S^μ)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:piece-a-specht-character-trace","label":"lem:piece-a-specht-character-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/piece-a-specht-character-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.centralC2_mapsTo_specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.centralC2_mapsTo_specht","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PieceASpechtCharacter.lean#L32-L42","doc":"The endomorphism `ρ(C₂) = (Mtab.rep μ).asAlgebraHom (centralC2 …)` maps the\nSpecht submodule `S^μ` into itself: on `S^μ` it acts by the scalar `contentSqSum μ`\n(`centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum`), and `S^μ` is closed under that scalar. This is\nthe invariance hypothesis needed to `LinearMap.restrict` `ρ(C₂)` to `S^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}